{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon","id":92008,"title":"Biggest Fails/Ups/D'ouhs on the OWoD Cannon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-15T18:28:26-07:00","id":92008,"title":"Biggest Fails/Ups/D'ouhs on the OWoD Cannon","content":"OK, Listen/read carefully. i dont mean writter's mistakes or anything like that. i mean events whithin the WoD cannon that you concider it deserved a facepalm or only worsen things or managed to get everything more FUBAR.<br /> <br /> on my end , im having a though one between<br /> A ) Hermetics creating a new vampire clan<br /> B ) technocracy going doctor strangelove on ravnos<br /> C ) Technocracy going doctor strangelove on the Oblivion<br /> <br /> which ones you concider the biggest facepalms within the cannon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T19:13:23-07:00","id":92029,"title":"","content":"I've got a decent gripe with how the 6th Great Maelstrom played out as well. Not human chaos (LIKE EVERY OTHER MAELSTROM), nor from a war breaking out in the Underworld (which would rapidly feed Oblivion, likely causing a Maelstrom), but instead from a convoluted chain of events that hinges on several other game lines. Ugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T20:21:00-07:00","id":92065,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Crowley;n92008]<br /> A ) Hermetics creating a new vampire clan/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I will always go with option A. To such an extent as this usually never happened in games I run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T21:23:44-07:00","id":92101,"title":"","content":"Noddism as truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T22:02:14-07:00","id":92112,"title":"","content":"I think the confession of Old Man Laughing Many Skins on Apocalypse was a massive facepalm for everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T22:40:13-07:00","id":92130,"title":"","content":"Actually the Technocracy wasn't responsible for the 6GM. The short version is that the Anubis called in a favor the Ferrymen owed him to have them convince the Hierarchy to attack and destroy Enoch, the Relic-city of Caine's First City that served as the HQ of the True Black Hand. While they were laying siege to the city the Dark Kingdom of Jade, aided by the traitor Smiling Lord, began their invasion. To end the siege quickly the Hierarchy chose to use the Relics of Fat Man and Little Boy, the atomic bombs that ended WWII. It worked. Unfortunately it sent shockwaves through the Underworld. At that time a VE working for and spying on a group known as the Orphic Circle arranged for him to conduct an experiment involving the detonation of a nuke in the Labyrinth. But as he was still preparing his nuke the shockwaves from Enoch triggered it prematurely. The Technocracy itself had no hand in the 6GM. It was not their experiment nor did they have any part in provoking the conflicts in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T01:08:13-07:00","id":92175,"title":"","content":"I think Baba yaga &amp; shadow curtain -storyline were pretty badly done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T02:12:48-07:00","id":92188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=92130#post92130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the Technocracy wasn't responsible for the 6GM. The short version is that the Anubis called in a favor the Ferrymen owed him to have them convince the Hierarchy to attack and destroy Enoch, the Relic-city of Caine's First City that served as the HQ of the True Black Hand. While they were laying siege to the city the Dark Kingdom of Jade, aided by the traitor Smiling Lord, began their invasion. To end the siege quickly the Hierarchy chose to use the Relics of Fat Man and Little Boy, the atomic bombs that ended WWII. It worked. Unfortunately it sent shockwaves through the Underworld. At that time a VE working for and spying on a group known as the Orphic Circle arranged for him to conduct an experiment involving the detonation of a nuke in the Labyrinth. But as he was still preparing his nuke the shockwaves from Enoch triggered it prematurely. The Technocracy itself had no hand in the 6GM. It was not their experiment nor did they have any part in provoking the conflicts in the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div> Even worse. I don't like three other games (Vampire, Mage, Mummy) having integral parts in a major Wraith event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T05:51:53-07:00","id":92249,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair it was only one mage, working for a group of vampires, mages, sorcerers, mediums and others obsessed with Death and the Underworld that already existed in WtO. So I wouldn't really consider MtAs as playing a major role in the 6GM. With Enoch I think that was more them trying to get rid of some of the lingering bits of the infamous <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i>.<br /> <br /> But the most important thing about the Week of Nightmares, the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the Avatar Storm is that they are the build up to the Time of Judgment and are the signs that everything is beginning to fall apart for <i>everyone</i>. I get the sense that they didn't want these events to solely affect one line but rather things that affected everyone or at least as many as possible. With the WoN the Technocracy got involved several days after [Ravnos] started his rampage and was battling several of the oldest Kuei-Jin Bodhisattva. That's not something the Technocracy can just ignore or send HIT Mark kill teams to eradicate them. It was basically a group of vampire blood gods fighting each other, oblivious to everyone dying around them. The 6GM did more than just ravage the Underworld, it directly created DtF, MtR and HtR, and had an impact on Orpheus's setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T08:07:22-07:00","id":92283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=92112#post92112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the confession of Old Man Laughing Many Skins on Apocalypse was a massive facepalm for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall where that was in Apocalypse. Could you help someone out with a page number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T10:25:54-07:00","id":92346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=92283#post92283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't recall where that was in Apocalypse. Could you help someone out with a page number?</div> </div> </div> </div>a friend told me that on his story, he traveled as a shapeshifter (joining every shapeshifter on the WtA mythos) to learn the ultimate secret, in the end of days he gets killed. his last words are &quot;T-the secret..is...Hehehe....&quot; and then he dies. i havent read it, but thats what my ST friend told me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T11:10:26-07:00","id":92365,"title":"","content":"I know Old Man Manyskins is in the Nuwisha Breedbook as well as the Werewolf the Wild West but I've never heard of his death. Is it in one of the Apocalypse end times scenarios or something? :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T11:22:50-07:00","id":92370,"title":"","content":"i belive so","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T07:34:46-07:00","id":92779,"title":"","content":"Samuel. Haight.<br /> <br /> EDIT: OR, the <i>Revised</i>-era shift in the Mage continuity that tried to force the game (inasmuch as shifts in the metaplot can force anyone to do anything in their own, individual games) into low magic mode. Basically anyone who got into the game really enjoying the umbra ships, and off-world colonies, HIT Marks, bug hunts, what-have-you, were faced with either not having any new content to fit their game, or to change their games in accordance with the shift. So, yeah, no one was forced to run their games in any particular manner, but at the same time, if they wanted to keep running the game in that 2ed. style, there pretty much wasn't any new content appropriate to that setting ever again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 03-17-2014, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T08:38:45-07:00","id":92805,"title":"","content":"Mummy Revised in its entirety. Mummy 2nd Edition was a really cool addition to nearly any sphere you cared to cross it with, but Revised Mummy is bland and way to far up its own ass to fit with anything else. That and the whole idea of the half-human half other thing as been done to death. It worked well in Demon and debatably functionally in Changeling, but mummies were their own thing and they fit just fine. Not to mention the fact that Mummy Revised, not content with screwing up its own sphere, felt the need to destroy the Children of Osiris from Vampire as well.<br /> <br /> Also, this one will probably be unpopular as I seem to be one of the very few who actually liked Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, but the retcon of the origins of Vicissitude. I thought the bizarre sentient Umbral disease was a really cool story (the Souleaters as presented are a bit silly, but that part is easily removed without blowing up the whole storyline).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T09:37:21-07:00","id":92840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>killersquirrel59</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=92805#post92805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to be one of the very few who actually liked Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</div> </div> </div> </div> Love that book. You are not alone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T02:10:17-07:00","id":93320,"title":"","content":"The &quot;canon&quot; ending to what happened to Baba Yaga is the biggest Fail I can think of for CWOD. I really enjoyed the Baba Yaga Shadow Curtain schtik, and the whole railroad adventure where you find out she wasn't this cool character just some senile old loser destined to fail... kind of ruined everything cool from Rage Across Russia. I mean compare how it was Handled to how Death of Blacktooth was Handled. The Death of Blacktooth is applauded because its the epitome example of hey we leave up to the ST in case you want your players to be the ones responsible.<br /> <br /> So I ignored the To Grandmother's house we go story.<br /> <br /> Seriously how lame is it to just say naaaw Baba Yaga is helpless against another Methuselah just because she is younger LOLZ.... And naturally this was also that one place where we get the evidence that Cainites are over 14k years old...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T02:11:33-07:00","id":93321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=92112#post92112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the confession of Old Man Laughing Many Skins on Apocalypse was a massive facepalm for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Confession?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T04:03:52-07:00","id":93370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=93320#post93320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I ignored the To Grandmother's house we go story.<br /> <br /> Seriously how lame is it to just say naaaw Baba Yaga is helpless against another Methuselah just because she is younger LOLZ.... And naturally this was also that one place where we get the evidence that Cainites are over 14k years old...</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was a very weak adventure myself. The elements were good, the punk-out for Baba Yaga was anticlimactic and embodied a lot of what was bad about the metaplot (players as spectators - could have been a very interesting &quot;Elder chess&quot; scenario with the PCs as free-willed pawns). Has my vote for a facepalm moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:23:19-07:00","id":93609,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was so much nuking Ravnos so much as nuking India and not having anyone notice that was the real problem. Vicissitude as an alien/spiritual disease was perfectly cool in my mind. What wasn't cool was trees with Vicissitude. Likewise before certain other aspects of the game were hammered out more firmly there is a fiction piece featuring ghouled ducks. Gypsies was retconned, so magical racism would have to weight until the Year of the Lotus. Berlin by Night was retconned, so no vampire snakes and no vampire Himmler. Some of the decisions on how get rid of Crafts for Mage Revised bordered on racist. Jamming Asian Crafts into the Akashics whether or not they fit seemed...off. Pentex seems to meander between believable villainy, outright-parody, and Captain Planet style villainy all in the same book. I tended to pay little attention to things like characters and modules though, and I think that's where most of the really derpy stuff came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:36:54-07:00","id":93625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=93609#post93609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it was so much nuking Ravnos so much as nuking India and not having anyone notice that was the real problem. Vicissitude as an alien/spiritual disease was perfectly cool in my mind. What wasn't cool was trees with Vicissitude. Likewise before certain other aspects of the game were hammered out more firmly there is a fiction piece featuring ghouled ducks. Gypsies was retconned, so magical racism would have to weight until the Year of the Lotus. Berlin by Night was retconned, so no vampire snakes and no vampire Himmler. Some of the decisions on how get rid of Crafts for Mage Revised bordered on racist. Jamming Asian Crafts into the Akashics whether or not they fit seemed...off. Pentex seems to meander between believable villainy, outright-parody, and Captain Planet style villainy all in the same book. I tended to pay little attention to things like characters and modules though, and I think that's where most of the really derpy stuff came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well actually they Nuked Bangladesh, but from the outside the rest of the World thought it was just the Typhoon of the Millenium that killed like over a hundred thousand people, and the Technocracy discredited supernatural sightings by claiming gas leaks from the property damage made the superstitious locals hallucinate. And to be fair there were constant storms going on as Chaos ensued from the Penumbra being over excited, Antediluvian level Chimeristry making real illusions of Storms and Demons, and the Hsien summoning Stormclouds to block out the Sun so the 3 Bodhisattvas didn't have to worry about Sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T11:50:12-07:00","id":93643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=92840#post92840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Love that book. You are not alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked it as well. Mixed feelings on the Souleaters, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T01:59:35-07:00","id":95466,"title":"","content":"White Wolf's biggest mistake in the classic World of Darkness was hastily cramming the various supernatural populations onto a single planet and then clumsily backpedaling to erect and maintain extremely contrived separations that strain credibility. The largest strain to credibility was having global supernatural superpowers like elder vampires, the Technocracy, and Pentex all on the same planet yet somehow not in constant conflict with each other over territory and resources. (I posted my solution to that as the thread <i>A More Logical World of Darkness</i>.) Relatedly, White Wolf's second biggest mistake was not ubiquitously and consistently utilizing either the atheistic Metaphysic Trinity and/or the theistic Triat as a background tenet to weave all of the elements of the World of Darkness into a cohesive whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2509-thanateros","name":"Thanateros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T18:03:19-07:00","id":137425,"title":"","content":"<i>*clears throat*</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Midnight Circus</span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">*Drops Mic*<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*I try not to acknowledge Gypsy in polite conversation...</span></span></i></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2599-professor-absinthe","user":"Professor Absinthe","date":". 05-14-2014, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2599-professor-absinthe","name":"Professor Absinthe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2599_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T18:48:47-07:00","id":137475,"title":"","content":"My picks for the top 10....<br /> <br /> 1. The Week of Nightmares<br /> 2. Gangrel leaving the Camarilla<br /> 3. The Avatar Storm<br /> 4. Stargazers leaving the Garou Nation<br /> 5. The entire existence of Demon: The Fallen and to a lesser extent, Kindred of the East<br /> 6. Wiping out the Children of Osiris<br /> 7. Hunter: The Reckoning<br /> 8. Lodin's death<br /> 9. The ham-fisted &quot;one-true wayism&quot; omnipresent in Revised Edition. (Your Mileage May Vary on this one)<br /> 10. New York By Night (for that matter, why in the hell would the Sabbat control New York at all in the first place?)<br /> <br /> Revised Edition in general kinda sucked for me. There was some good stuff in it, and it was the best mechanically until V20 came along, but I find a lot of my facepalm moments with cWoD canon are in Revised Edition, with the exception of Lodin's death. Now, this is my opinion, and to be fair, I do enjoy Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, I like katanas, and I use <i>Senshi: The Merchandising</i> as part of my own personal head-canon for Classic World of Darkness, so take my words with a grain of salt. So, if you like Revised Edition, that's okay. I just personally didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T07:45:22-07:00","id":138046,"title":"","content":"A couple caveats here - I always run crossover games of some sort (even when all PCs are one type), and I never upgraded past 2nd edition (because Mage 2nd was the best).<br /> <br /> <u>Avatar Storm</u><br /> It wasn't the storm itself, per se, but the whole idea behind it. For some reason (I know it's been debated, but it doesn't matter) they decided to basically fuck up the entire Mage setting in one fell swoop. Easily the dumbest thing they ever did, canon-wise. <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Tremere</u><br /> This is something that always bothered me. Not because of the backstory involved (although that too was questionable), but because of the consequence. I detest the idea of &quot;vampire wizards&quot;, preferring instead for each of the main 5 lines I used in my games (MtA, WtA, VtM, CtD, WtO) to have their own distinct flavors. It just never sat well with me.. although for some of my friends Tremere were the greatest thing since sliced bread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Hunter: the Reckoning</u><br /> I will also have to admit that I never played this game. I didn't buy it when it came out, and it wasn't until years later when a buddy of mine had fallen in love with it that I ever even bothered to find out what it was about. What really got me here was the sheer audacity of characters with abilities that could prevent True Magick and kill supernaturals being called normal mortals. I also don't really understand (to this very day) how Hunters fit into the metaphysics of the WoD without being brutally obvious or almost ST Fiat. I'm sure my ignorance here is a huge factor, but the whole premise never made any sense to me whatsoever. Mortal hunters are fine, I use them in my games (especially historical settings) all the time. Mortal hunters with powers greater than True Magick is... confusing. The whole thing seems like &quot;Mage: the Ascension, version 0.5&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:25:37-07:00","id":138146,"title":"","content":"I've got beef with how the Week of Nightmares went down. You have one of the defining Vampire metaplot moments, but the only Kindred involved die en masse, while Kuei-Jin and the Technocracy steal the spotlight. I don't like crossover focus in major plot events, y'know? Why not have the Sabbat do what the Sabbat exist to do and throw themselves at that Antediluvian as the army they've always dreamed of being?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:14:47-07:00","id":138385,"title":"","content":"Little can beat Berlin By Night:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Heinrich_Himmler\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Heinrich_Himmler</a><br /> <br /> Sabbat Tremere anti-tribu Himmler","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:08:39-07:00","id":138460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=138385#post138385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little can beat Berlin By Night:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Heinrich_Himmler\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Heinrich_Himmler</a><br /> <br /> Sabbat Tremere anti-tribu Himmler</div> </div> </div> </div>And with that...My whole setting changes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T04:32:07-07:00","id":139192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=138385#post138385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Little can beat Berlin By Night: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Heinrich_Himmler\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Heinrich_Himmler</a> Sabbat Tremere anti-tribu Himmler</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to confess, I always secretly wondered if the destruction of the Tremere Antitribu in the Transylvania Chronicles was just an elaborate way for the writers to get rid of this guy without actually having to acknowledge his existence again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T05:37:21-07:00","id":139212,"title":"","content":"The entire cannon ending for the Wraith and Changeling systems. Bespoke of the inability for White-Wolf to properly finish what they started. The reasons these systems couldn't get revised editions seemed to be more monetarily based than important naturally directed plot resolution. It'd be like watching The Hobbit story end with the Desolation of Smaug. Rocks fall everyone dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  I forgot to give props to the monkeys 05-16-2014, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:06:37-07:00","id":139664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I have to confess, I always secretly wondered if the destruction of the Tremere Antitribu in the Transylvania Chronicles was just an elaborate way for the writers to get rid of this guy without actually having to acknowledge his existence again.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> Either turned into ash or ashtray, the fate of disgracing characters.</span></span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:24:24-07:00","id":139724,"title":"","content":"I'd second Vampire Himmler. It's not just how silly the basic idea is, it's that they don't even do anything with the concept. He's just in Berlin hanging out.<br /> <br /> least that's how I remember it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T15:12:28-07:00","id":139864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=139212#post139212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire cannon ending for the Wraith and Changeling systems. Bespoke of the inability for White-Wolf to properly finish what they started. The reasons these systems couldn't get revised editions seemed to be more monetarily based than important naturally directed plot resolution. It'd be like watching The Hobbit movie end with the Desolation of Smaug. Rocks fall everyone dies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Changeling get a full write-up in <i>Time of Judgment</i> like the other limited lines? <br /> <br /> I've got plenty of beef with how Wraith ended, but at least we got Orpheus out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T19:03:09-07:00","id":140144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=139864#post139864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but at least we got Orpheus out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it did. A shame Orpheus isn't as appreciated as it should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T19:59:26-07:00","id":140169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=139864#post139864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't Changeling get a full write-up in <i>Time of Judgment</i> like the other limited lines?<br /> <br /> I've got plenty of beef with how Wraith ended, but at least we got Orpheus out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they did... So did Wraith. Was it meant to end there originally? No. Not from the ammount of material that was on the drawing boards for Wraith and Changeling both that never got finished. But that's what happens when money and time and other's decisions override what makes a good plotline. Imagine the ST for your game taking you through 7 adventures leaving you clues for more to come all along the way and then wraps your game up in one session with a big war and takes off with a new group to play something else. It totally happens and life can be that way, but you're still left hanging and feeling like it was all over too quick.<br /> <br /> But yeah I do agree about Orpheus. That was a pleasant surprise for me. Doesn't make up for the rest though. It's canon now. Not likely to change even if there's Anniversary editions, but here's hoping there's a bit more resolution than &quot;one splat to cover them all&quot; Time of Judgement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T08:42:48-07:00","id":141612,"title":"","content":"There is one more horrible thing I uncovered. Jan Pieterzoon has to feed on... rape victims. And when Sabbat eliminated his herd, he arranged a rape of a random woman through Dominate. How the hell he has Humanity of 6?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T10:38:11-07:00","id":141685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=140169#post140169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah I do agree about Orpheus. That was a pleasant surprise for me. Doesn't make up for the rest though. It's canon now. Not likely to change even if there's Anniversary editions, but here's hoping there's a bit more resolution than &quot;one splat to cover them all&quot; Time of Judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if there's one book that really frustrates me it's <i>Time of Judgement</i>. It feels so half-assed and incomplete compared to every other gameline ending books, WtO's Ends of Empire, the Big Three and Orpheus's End Game. Worse there are good and even great things in the book but they're either surrounded by bad material and/or underdeveloped and lacking the punch of other books' end of days scenarios. For instance I <i>love</i> the opening fiction of the HtR section, it really sets the tone for a ToJ HtR chronicle and if I ever ran one I'd copy the pages and hand them out over the course of it to help sell the feeling of the world as we know it coming to an end. But what follows it is horribly underwhelming, much of it being stuff that anyone could have come up with, and making the Imbued feel so small and insignificant compared to everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T11:17:01-07:00","id":141717,"title":"","content":"In cannon &quot; What were you thinking?!&quot; moments<br /> 1) &quot;Hey I'm kind of worried about House Tremere, shouldn't we look into this a little bit more?&quot;<br /> &quot;Nah, I'm sure their fine, nothing big ever happens in Austria anyway...&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;So the commoner leadership wants to meet and discuss terms before the situation breaks out into all out war that could kill us all and destroy whats left of the dreaming at worst and at best cause a rift between the sidhe and everyone else that will last for generations and possibly hasten the arrival of the endless winter..&quot;<br /> &quot;Fuck that lets stab them with Iron.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) &quot;Why hello Wendigo, nice piece of land you got here...&quot;<br /> <br /> 4) &quot;Hey guys lets all prove how awsome we are by going into the heart of spiritual corruption and destroy it. when we're done everyone will know the name White Howlers!&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Cappaodicous: &quot;I'm really thinking this Augustus Giovanni is a promising young fellow, maybey we should bring him and his entire family into the fold.&quot;<br /> His progeny: &quot;My Lord are you sure that's a good idea, they kind of have a reputation for being less than trustworthy and seem more interested in temperal power than learning the secrets of death for its own sake.&quot;<br /> &quot;it'll be fine they'll fit right in.&quot;<br /> <br /> 6)Technocrat: &quot;hey I wonder what happens when you take this nuclear warhead and throw it at the edge of the Abyss...&quot;<br /> <br /> 7) Hermetic Student: &quot;you know those Craft Masons are making some pretty good arguments, and they are gaining some pretty heavy support, shouldn't we you know, at least listen to what they have to say?&quot;<br /> Hermetic Master: &quot;Pfft. Peasants!&quot; *looks out windows and lobs fireballs* &quot;Get back to your Turnips!&quot;<br /> <br /> Out of Game:<br /> White Wolf developer: &quot;hey guys! i got this great idea for a supplement about the Roma as a people!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T12:46:38-07:00","id":141742,"title":"","content":"For me many come from mage.<br /> <br /> 1) In the Sons of the Ether book, two mages travel by super awesome car to the umbra and there oldest mage tell the young one of a plane they are crossing which is an alternate earth in which Tesla is alive and everything is a Utopia of SCIENCE!! and individuality and finish by saying that before the avatar storm mages could travel and remain there indefinitely. So that raises the question WHY THE HELL WERE THERE ANY SONS OF THE ETHER ON EARTH BEFORE THE AVATAR STORM? why didn't all pack their stuff and went to this utopia and left this rotten mud-ball of a plane to rot. No, seriously why would you stay here? Utopia or being hunted by technocracy yeah tough call that one.<br /> <br /> 2) Nazi movement. Almost all the material goes a great length to assure us that the nazi movement wasn't supernatural in origin that like the 9/11 it was people being people and that suggesting otherwise would be a disrespect. And the Verbena revised say &quot;oh yeah, there is this sub group name rune crafters, they basically gave the nazis the push they needed&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) The perfect metis. A metis born <u><b>without any defect.</b></u> Picture in the book: a metis with horns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-18-2014, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T01:14:09-07:00","id":142153,"title":"","content":"I was going to say &quot;Tremere in the Mirror&quot;... but then I got to thinking about it, and that wasn't SO bad. Kinda dumb, but whatever. Then i thought, &quot;Second massassa War,&quot; and I'm like, well, okay, but it gave the Order of Hermes something to do at least... &quot; So maybe the idea of &quot;suddenly everyone hates the Salubri,&quot; and then it struck me!<br /> <br /> The Tremere are the rock-bottom, ultimate, concise answer to every question that even lightly touches on &quot;Worst idea in the oWoD&quot;<br /> <br /> - They are the $5 hookers of the game's metaplot.They are <i>everywhere</i>. And like the girlfriend character of a bad ST, they are instrumental to everything without ever being THAT interesting or even involved - it all just goes their way because!<br /> - They warp two entire game lines, Vampire and Mage. Thank goodness for the Tzimisce and Setites, else they'd be mutating werewolf as well, I'm sure. Seriously, Vampire's a game of mysteries, and supposedly the Antedilluvians are one of them, oh, except for the one time a wizard ate one. Oh yeah, there's wizards too. That's why we call them Usurpers. Despite of course Antedilluvians not existing, hurp-a-durp.<br /> - Thaumaturgy.<br /> - <i>THAUMATURGY</i>.<br /> - No, seriously, I have never seen a Vampire game where the ST did not put up Thaumaturgy roadblocks. It's a Discipline that only one clan gets, but it's like thirty other Disciplines too an it has these rituals and here's how you can develop your own paths that do whatever the hell you want and on and on and on. <i>Conceptually</i>, it's not terrible, I kinda dig the idea of vampire sorcerers. But... were I to go back to write this stuff, I would actually take a cue from KoE, give the Tremere some sort of undead variation of the five (four?) elements, and there's their Thaumaturgy paths; everyone can learn rituals.<br /> - The fact that I just said &quot;I would replace Thaumaturgy with stuff from Kindred of the East,&quot; and probably few people will be outraged by that is another point that the Tremere are pretty bad.<br /> - The whole &quot;poof!&quot; of the Tremere antitribu. Okay, the clan is a bad idea, so I guess I can't complain about them being <i>fewer</i> of them... Especially when the ones missing are Sabbat. But plot-wise, this is just unfulfilling on any level.<br /> - The Salubri. Not my favorite clan. But the whole Tremere / Salubri thing just turns the Salubri into these goofy <i>things</i>, where you either have humming monks so saccharine that they would make the Children of Gaia vomit, or you have the &quot;screw Vampire I want to play D&amp;D!&quot; antitribu... Or I guess, the whole Nkulu Zao thing. And another thing. You have <i>four bloodlines</i> of this very distinctive clan. Hell, maybe more, it seems like every book snuck in a salubri flavor - but they're all in hiding from the Tremere! It's just the silliest damn thing.<br /> - The Gehenna Scenario where Tremere himself hinges the fate of his plan... on Mormon Genealogical records. You know there's no excuse here. Gehenna came out in 2004. The Human genome Project was completed in 2001 and had begun in 1990. Tremere's.... <i>supposed to be</i> a smart guy, and he's going to hinge his plan for world domination on the shoddy records of people who think posthumously baptizing Albert Einstein makes him a Mormon in heaven? Okay so this isn't actually the fault of the Tremere so much as bad writing, but... still, they went with the tremere, which at least underlines hte point.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah. Tremere. The game wouldn't miss them if they were gone, and would probably be smarter if they had never been there.<br /> <br /> Second place... the utter <i>insistence</i> of screwing the silver Fangs out of the Apocalypse and handing it to Koneitziko. Really? <i>Really</i>? We'd been following Albrecht and his pack since the <i>1st edition core book</i>, several novels, sourcebook after sourcebook, and oh by the way screw that the title goes to this side character we decided to make prominent at the 11th hour. YAY! Really, that's just some bait-and-switch bullshit. I actually kind of consider the revised-era Shadow Lords sort of like I do the Tremere, because they became this trashy Mary Sue, right-about-everything, we-have-no-flaws-except-being-TOO-Awesome, nu metal dark and edgy good guys bullshit thing going... And in every apocalypse scenario, not only does Albrecht get canned - and not in any dynamic way, never with an achievement, always just &quot;Oh, I guess he's dead now - but the <i>entire tribe goes with him</i>. we literally spend three editions working up to the Fangs actually getting their crap together, and rallying under strong leadership but NOPE Girlfriend Character steps in and neuters all that BECAUSE!<br /> <br /> And third place is Changeling. <i>Sigh</i>. I'm not sure exactly what one specific thing here, but towards the end... David disappearing could be a good plot hook. Too bad it was a repetitive one (Charon, Horus / Osiris, Lucifer...) but worse, <i>they kept telling us exactly what happened</i>. There was no mystery there. Meilge had him abducted, bludgeoned, and caged, then forced him to abdicate. it's all right there in the text. That's not how you write a political thriller! But in itself, <i>it's not a bad idea</i>. it makes perfect sense, scheming nobles against a king they dislike, perfect sense. No, probably the real sin here was turning Changeling into Space Werewolf.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Space werewolf?</i>&quot; you ask, with a puzzled look on your face. yes. Space werewolf.<br /> <br /> Look, we had two closing arcs to Changeling. One was the King David thing. Okay, like I said, not a terrible idea despite the execution. The next... is the Rise of the Fomorians, with the Casque of Sorrows and all that. Which basically means that Changeling turns int oa game about your characters in a world-defining battle against ultimate evil and its servants who want to crush the universe under the tentacles, and only one final battle can you see where this is going, right? You even get Book of Lost houses, which is pretty much all about those five houses being heralds of what's coming and trying to rally the other changelings against the Apocaohwait. There's even TWO Time of Judgement Scenarios for Changeling that make the &quot;Ragnarok&quot; scenario from Apocalypse look low-key.<br /> <br /> So yeah, one of the ending arcs of Changeling, has you basically playing werewolf, only you're in the Dreaming. Werewolf in Space. Which I imagine is like what happens if you were to do a Game of Thrones / Barbarella mashup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 05-19-2014, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T06:10:54-07:00","id":142243,"title":"","content":"Okay here is another one that isn't so much fluff as it is crunch.<br /> <br /> Arch-Spheres.<br /> <br /> I never used these, as I felt they were ridiculous. It felt tacked on and as if it did not fit the already existing Sphere mechanics at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T12:54:53-07:00","id":142615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=141742#post141742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The perfect metis. A metis born <u><b>without any defect.</b></u> Picture in the book: a metis with horns</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, <b>Apocalypse</b>. Quoted from the book: <b>Gifts:</b> Horns of the Impaler and listed as a &quot;Possessed Black Spiral Dancer&quot; under Wyrmspawn. If he had different stats for Weaver, Wyld, or Gaia, I'm sure he would be different for each of them.<br /> And it's been said before that falling to the Wyrm usually does give you some defects even if you weren't born with them.<br /> <br /> I've got one! Read about the CoG characters, what they do and what comes out of their mouths in the Children of Gaia Revised Tribebook... *Bangs head on desk*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:08:49-07:00","id":142628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thanateros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=95466#post95466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf's biggest mistake in the classic World of Darkness was hastily cramming the various supernatural populations onto a single planet and then clumsily backpedaling to erect and maintain extremely contrived separations that strain credibility. The largest strain to credibility was having global supernatural superpowers like elder vampires, the Technocracy, and Pentex all on the same planet yet somehow not in constant conflict with each other over territory and resources. (I posted my solution to that as the thread <i>A More Logical World of Darkness</i>.) Relatedly, White Wolf's second biggest mistake was not ubiquitously and consistently utilizing either the atheistic Metaphysic Trinity and/or the theistic Triat as a background tenet to weave all of the elements of the World of Darkness into a cohesive whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Deciding everything is now a crossover is not a way to handle crossover options. Instead, there should have been a book about conversions and how to do it.<br /> <br /> On that note: Bygone Bestiary. What is <i>up </i>with some of the backstories of these creatures? The constantly-weeping cows that hit on women come to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T13:58:40-07:00","id":142661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=142615#post142615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, <b>Apocalypse</b>. Quoted from the book: <b>Gifts:</b> Horns of the Impaler and listed as a &quot;Possessed Black Spiral Dancer&quot; under Wyrmspawn. If he had different stats for Weaver, Wyld, or Gaia, I'm sure he would be different for each of them.<br /> And it's been said before that falling to the Wyrm usually does give you some defects even if you weren't born with them.<br /> <br /> I've got one! Read about the CoG characters, what they do and what comes out of their mouths in the Children of Gaia Revised Tribebook... *Bangs head on desk*</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, checking my version you are right. My confusion came from the first part of the book which describes the perfect metis as born without any defect and then i jumped to character sheet and i miss he had that gift. My bad.<br /> <br /> Do you have a physical copy of the book or a PDF? I have a print version and i cannot find the death of old man many skins. Do you know where it is by any chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T14:50:33-07:00","id":142687,"title":"","content":"A hiccup that's always bugged me: why were the Giovanni not hated and hunted like the Tremere? The Cappadocians were far better liked than the Salubri and the crime was the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T01:36:31-07:00","id":143190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=142687#post142687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hiccup that's always bugged me: why were the Giovanni not hated and hunted like the Tremere? The Cappadocians were far better liked than the Salubri and the crime was the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really didn't make sense to me how it was even possible. The Cappadocians were a widespread Clan and the events related to the Giovanni were so geographically isolated, how on earth was it possible to eliminate the Cappadocians in such a short amount of time and so completely?<br /> <br /> Also, from a creative angle, they are too close to Tremere. The Tremere already have the tightly knit Clan of usurper sorcerer diablerists well and covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T02:42:28-07:00","id":143239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It really didn't make sense to me how it was even possible. The Cappadocians were a widespread Clan and the events related to the Giovanni were so geographically isolated, how on earth was it possible to eliminate the Cappadocians in such a short amount of time and so completely? </div> </div> </div>One user I PMed with had Cappadocians survive in East Asia intact since Giovanni purge did not reach them due to geographical reasons (with assumption Kuei-Jins are replaced with Cainites and have local variations of every Clan except Tremere and Giovanni who are a recent European development). Thinking of that, Cappadocians should survive in Africa too, but I'm no expert on Laibon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T03:16:37-07:00","id":143260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=143239#post143239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking of that, Cappadocians should survive in Africa too, but I'm no expert on Laibon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canon-wise they do (the Mia Watu). I think the best sense way to look at the Giovanni takeover is that it happens when everyone else is distracted by the Anarch revolt, and largely beheads the Cappadocians as a Clan in the West (Antediluvian and majority of Methuselahs) rather than outright destroying them worldwide. It also helps give a more general explanation for the number of &quot;Cappadocian in a funny hat&quot; bloodlines still around in the modern day (off the top of my head: Mia Watu, Samedi and Harbingers). Anyone who was hard to get at (in the Shadowlands/in Africa/in the Caribbean), got overlooked.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 05-20-2014, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T03:22:57-07:00","id":143266,"title":"","content":"I assume then Lamians were enough concentrated in Europe and its immediate neighborhood to get shanked completely by Giovanni?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T03:40:14-07:00","id":143289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=143266#post143266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume then Lamians were enough concentrated in Europe and its immediate neighborhood to get shanked completely by Giovanni?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've never seen another mention of them (or anything like them) outside Europe and their stragglers are explicitly noted as being bloodhunted out of existence by the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T04:21:24-07:00","id":143298,"title":"","content":"Biggest &quot;urgh&quot; moments for me:<ul><li>The progression towards Gehenna/Apocalypse etc. (ie. &quot;It's here now! See the signs!&quot;) Not necessary (save for book sales) and actively harmful to most of the settings as opposed to beneficial. Masquerade in particular was stronger thematically when Gehenna was a superstitious seeming Sword of Damocles for Elders rather than an increasingly unassailable fact.</li> <li>The Gehenna/Apocalypse/ToJ books - I can understand the desire to give a wrap up to the gamelines (and there are some cool ideas in them) but the &quot;choose your own ending&quot; approach wasn't very satisfying. On top of that, if you build up events as &quot;the ultimate&quot; for a decade, you're doomed to create expectations you can never fulfill no matter how well written you make it.</li> <li>A lot of the &quot;sense of change&quot; events in the lines were actively harmful to the settings for little real benefit - Malkavians all having Dementation made them less interesting, Gangrel leaving the Camarilla, Ravnos Clan-wipeout, and so on. A real pity as a lot of the later books were better in tune with the settings aside from these kind of things.</li> <li>Related to the previous point - The low payoff destruction of fairly important canon elements. For example, Baba Yaga's bizarre worfing (doubly objectionable as it nicks and mangles elements of Russian folklore at the same time), and the offscreen wipeout of the Tremere Antitribu (not necessarily bad that they went, but bad that they went in such a silly wasteful way).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T04:56:10-07:00","id":143314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Masquerade in particular was stronger thematically when Gehenna was a superstitious seeming Sword of Damocles for Elders rather than an increasingly unassailable fact. </div> </div> </div>As I ignore imminent Gehenna, I am tempted to run space opera Vampire one day, with younger Kindred in rush to stake claims at terraformed Mars and for example younger Ventrue claiming their domains in space industry. I assume extraterrestial elders would be of particularly high generations compared to Masquerade, players being capable of taking 9th to 13th Generation with the Generation background and being 14th Generation by default (some Caitiff, some not, I recall not all 14th Gens are thinblooded).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T05:51:38-07:00","id":143345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=143314#post143314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I ignore imminent Gehenna, I am tempted to run space opera Vampire one day, with younger Kindred in rush to stake claims at terraformed Mars and for example younger Ventrue claiming their domains in space industry. I assume extraterrestial elders would be of particularly high generations compared to Masquerade, players being capable of taking 9th to 13th Generation with the Generation background and being 14th Generation by default (some Caitiff, some not, I recall not all 14th Gens are thinblooded).</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at &quot;World of Future Darkness&quot; if you can get your hands on it. Old WW Magazine article crossbreeding Cyberpunk 2020 with Masquerade. Might be good for material for this (though tonally different?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":""