manity;<br /> 08. Vicissitude as an alien disease; <br /> 09. Any non-hostile relationship between garou and kindred;<br /> 10. Conservation movement, feminist, fascist / nazi or communist vampires (all kine ideologies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T11:16:29-07:00","id":143726,"title":"","content":"Hmm. The Wu Zao survived the destruction of the Salubri fairly well, I think; one might imagine a Cappadocian bloodline surviving in Asia as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T17:08:36-07:00","id":143954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> feminist (...) vampires </div> </div> </div>I'm fond of this fragment from the Sins of Blood (Revised edition):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The feminist movement has fostered a number of radical groups that prey upon their members. These organizations use cultic methods to isolate the women within them, impose belief structures, break down the ego, discourage contrary thinking and talk, and even violently impose loyalty. The term feminazi insults many women, with good reason. These groups do exist, but they're not healthy. Many have an embittered, rage-filled leader with enough charisma to spread her hatred among her followers. These organizations hide behind a mask of human right issues, and all the while, they're discouraging free thought and individuality among their own members. Members are either 100 % with or 100 % ostracized from the organisation. </div> </div> </div>The context was a discussion of blood cults, so I can only imagine stereotypical rabid feminists, childer and ghouls of their Kindred mistress <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If we port that to Werewolf, then certainly Banes are behind that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 05-20-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T17:53:14-07:00","id":143980,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Katsura;n143954]<br /> I'm fond of this fragment from the Sins of Blood (Revised edition):<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The context was a discussion of blood cults, so I can only imagine stereotypical rabid feminists, childer and ghouls of their Kindred mistress <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>If we port that to Werewolf, then certainly Banes are behind that.[</b>/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Probably not. But they would feed on it and grow powerful from it, making it worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T18:08:14-07:00","id":143994,"title":"","content":"And pop, we got Fomori. Or Wyrm tainted Black Furies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T01:03:06-07:00","id":144278,"title":"","content":"...Actually I <i>think</i> that the &quot;feminist vampires&quot; in question are the Ahrimanes. Anyone remember them? No? Yeah, can't blame you.<br /> <br /> However the idea of &quot;kine ideologies&quot; among vampires isn't a problem, since, y'know, vampires aren't space aliens, they are created from and live among humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T02:09:45-07:00","id":144307,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Gangrel Clan has probably largest number of off-shoots of all Full Clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T04:16:39-07:00","id":144343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=144278#post144278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Actually I <i>think</i> that the &quot;feminist vampires&quot; in question are the Ahrimanes. Anyone remember them? No? Yeah, can't blame you.<br /> <br /> However the idea of &quot;kine ideologies&quot; among vampires isn't a problem, since, y'know, vampires aren't space aliens, they are created from and live among humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>which is a shame because spiritus is the perfect discipline to play something like the Dead wolves version on masquerade.<br /> <br /> A kinfolk being embraced. Its not the most broken discipline but is so fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T04:26:25-07:00","id":144348,"title":"","content":"Well, first you would have first modify Ahrimanes to be able to Embrace Kinfolk directly. <br /> <br /> A group of power hungry Kinfolk who go a Cainite route instead of a Skin Dancer one could be interesting one. Possibly aiming to become a bloodline on their own just as Skin Dancer try to become a Tribe on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T06:33:44-07:00","id":144423,"title":"","content":"Top three;<br /> <br /> 1) Railroading the Revised editions of each game into an End Times plot. Should have saved that for supplements. Never had a shred of interest in the end time scenario.<br /> 2) The tonal shift between Mage 2nd and Mage Revised. The irony of the Technocracy being rewritten to be more sympathetic, and the Traditions being rewritten to be less is... astounding.<br /> 3) The Sabbat. Seriously. They were supposed to be a mysterious sect of vampires in opposition to the Camarilla. Instead, we get Palladium-style supplement creep. Better powers! Better Disciplines! More Clans! They don't even need Humanity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3078-coffee-zombie","name":"Coffee Zombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T06:39:43-07:00","id":144426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=144348#post144348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first you would have first modify Ahrimanes to be able to Embrace Kinfolk directly.<br /> <br /> A group of power hungry Kinfolk who go a Cainite route instead of a Skin Dancer one could be interesting one. Possibly aiming to become a bloodline on their own just as Skin Dancer try to become a Tribe on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what we did in our last game. I played a caitiff who used to be a kinfolk so he had spiritus and ogham. And remove the ahrimanes from the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coffee Zombie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=144423#post144423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Top three;<br /> 2) The tonal shift between Mage 2nd and Mage Revised. The irony of the Technocracy being rewritten to be more sympathetic, and the Traditions being rewritten to be less is... astounding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im curious as to why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-21-2014, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T06:48:24-07:00","id":144435,"title":"","content":"Not sure how the Sabbat were presented as in any way &quot;Better&quot; than the Camarilla?...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T06:53:50-07:00","id":144438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=144426#post144426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im curious as to why?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy, especially the NWO is a stand in for the Big Brother out of 1984. Rewriting history constantly to suit themselves, to bring history in line with Party needs.<br /> <br /> Entire forums are full of opinions on the tonal shift. I see no need to practice necromancy on the arguments that are, for all intents in purposes, moot. M20 will hopefully be it's own book with it's own ideas. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3078-coffee-zombie","name":"Coffee Zombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T08:56:20-07:00","id":144515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=144278#post144278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Actually I <i>think</i> that the &quot;feminist vampires&quot; in question are the Ahrimanes. Anyone remember them? No? Yeah, can't blame you.<br /> <br /> However the idea of &quot;kine ideologies&quot; among vampires isn't a problem, since, y'know, vampires aren't space aliens, they are created from and live among humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always considered the World of Darkness a too pessimistic and cynical place, specially when you consider it from the Kindred point of view. I can't see how any of the ideas of a previous life (human ideas) can still make sense, after the embrace. Atmosphere-wise, they should only make sense as illusions fostered by neonates. Now, pure ideas, or single concepts, like &quot;freedom&quot; or &quot;slavery&quot;, still do make sense, and that's why there's such a thing as the Anarch Movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:26:34-07:00","id":144709,"title":"","content":"I try to storytell WoD as a bittersweet place. Okay, tragedies happen, but there is still hope if people get together and try to do something about it.<br /> <br /> Technocracy and Traditions both have good points, and should be portrayed as such. Safer world or more dynamic world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thats what we did in our last game. I played a caitiff who used to be a kinfolk so he had spiritus and ogham. And remove the ahrimanes from the setting. </div> </div> </div>I would still keep Ahrimanes around, but rewrite them into particularly picky Gangrel bloodline who Embraces female Kinfolk. The same way as Noiads Embraced Sami, Anda Embraced Mongols and Lhiannan Pagans only.<br /> <br /> Spiritus is still Clan Discipline created by Ahrimanes, but less insular members of the bloodline divulged secrets and non-Ahrimane Kinfolk Cainites can access it given enough contacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 05-21-2014, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:35:52-07:00","id":144718,"title":"","content":"Nothing against a bloodline embracing only women or men, or people of a given ethnic background. Ancient traditions were not democracies, or based on gender / ethnic equality concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:41:26-07:00","id":144722,"title":"","content":"Ahrimanes would be, essentially, a local bloodline embracing from Uktena female Kinfolk. That would explain why they manifested spirit related Discipline, Uktena are pretty good about spirits even compared to other Tribes.<br /> <br /> Possibly people could introduce other bloodlines made of and recruiting from disgruntled Kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T20:06:30-07:00","id":154480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=142628#post142628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Deciding everything is now a crossover is not a way to handle crossover options. Instead, there should have been a book about conversions and how to do it.<br /> <br /> <b>On that note: Bygone Bestiary. What is <i>up </i>with some of the backstories of these creatures? The constantly-weeping cows that hit on women come to mind.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but that is a book I absolutely love because the horrible beasts and creatures are almost all taken from actual legends of that time- it does not really give much use for those creatures, and honestly the book has limited potential use the more I think of it, but I will always treasure that book for the Bishop Fish. He just wants to talk about the lord and savior, he does not understand how you can be amazed at him being a fish compared to Jesus dying for your sins. So much love as a gag character who is basically a sweet kind religious person with the most honestly sincere intentions, <i>but a fish</i>.<br /> <br /> Having a book about one specific race wins for me, though I feel like a lot of things I don't know about caused <i>World of Darkness: Gypsies</i> to be the book it was. Having a book look at the magic of different ethnic groups and cultures around the world? Awesome but hard to do well and even then comes with a world of potential issues since even if you are faithful and delicate in treatment you are still turning a people's faith into a game.<br /> <br /> Not sure where I stand on that beyond my love of other cultures and stance that someone should always do some research and be very, very, very careful in treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3161-goliath","name":"Goliath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:17:38-07:00","id":154802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coffee Zombie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=144423#post144423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat. Seriously. They were supposed to be a mysterious sect of vampires in opposition to the Camarilla. Instead, we get Palladium-style supplement creep. Better powers! Better Disciplines! More Clans! They don't even need Humanity!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! The Sabbat also have better Clan Weaknesses and more nutjob/wank material!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T07:47:10-07:00","id":154826,"title":"","content":"Dead Magic 2 treated different cultures and ethnicities with their magical practices in quite a mature and sensible way. I love that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T09:08:38-07:00","id":154875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=154826#post154826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dead Magic 2 treated different cultures and ethnicities with their magical practices in quite a mature and sensible way. I love that book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hopefully we end up with so much interest in things that we get a M20: Dead Magic because upon learning of Wraith 20th I now think that anything awesome is potentially in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3161-goliath","name":"Goliath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T11:44:45-07:00","id":155039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goliath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=154480#post154480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but that is a book I absolutely love because the horrible beasts and creatures are almost all taken from actual legends of that time- it does not really give much use for those creatures, and honestly the book has limited potential use the more I think of it, but I will always treasure that book for the Bishop Fish. He just wants to talk about the lord and savior, he does not understand how you can be amazed at him being a fish compared to Jesus dying for your sins. So much love as a gag character who is basically a sweet kind religious person with the most honestly sincere intentions, <i>but a fish</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, thank you, thank you so much for giving me knowledge about the bishop fish <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now the &quot;Fishop&quot; is gonna be the local leader of the chorist in my campaign <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-31-2014, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T08:47:01-07:00","id":260617,"title":"","content":"1 - Tremere as Mages turning into Vampires and somehow winning a war versus the WHOLE Order of Hermes, plus the Tzimisce while being based in Transylvania (Ceoris).<br /> 2 - Mithras, thousands of years old and more powerful than you can ever imagine, fights a pack of Garou, gets into thorpor and a passing by Assamite just drinks from him. (oversimplistic but still bugs me)<br /> 3 - Vicissitude as a disease.<br /> 4 - The never ending resurgence of new and useless bloodlines (because the Kyasid are sooooooooo interesting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T12:13:31-07:00","id":260843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=260617#post260617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - Mithras, thousands of years old and more powerful than you can ever imagine, fights a pack of Garou, gets into thorpor and a passing by Assamite just drinks from him. (oversimplistic but still bugs me)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't most of his power retconned into being the result of inhabitation by an Earthbound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T15:58:33-07:00","id":261023,"title":"","content":"I can't recall correctly, it's been years <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> my group gave up on WoD much to my dismay and consequently I haven't picked up a book in years. But to be honest I don't remember any relation to Earthbounds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T22:48:58-07:00","id":261117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=260617#post260617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (because the Kyasid are sooooooooo interesting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! Leave the Kiasyd alone. I've always liked that particular Bloodline, even when they had the ridiculous Discipline spread of Necromancy, Mytheceria and Obteneration, but they still are pretty much the only beings in WoD that can deal with the Fae on their own terms without Mists forcing them to forget their dealings. SO they at least serve a clear purpose, unlike Daughters of Cacophony for example or Ahrimanes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T16:31:52-07:00","id":261583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=260843#post260843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't most of his power retconned into being the result of inhabitation by an Earthbound?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like Tiamat than Mithras, but I'll confess to not being up on all the setting lore from Demon. Certainly the stat blocks I've seen didn't seem out of place for a three millenium old 4th generation vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T18:29:40-07:00","id":261634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=260617#post260617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Tremere as Mages turning into Vampires and somehow winning a war versus the WHOLE Order of Hermes, plus the Tzimisce while being based in Transylvania (Ceoris).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the complete ineptitude of all those enemies (you left out the Nosferatu and Gangrel btw) to destroy a handful of fledling kindred completely without any magic whatsoever is a much bigger cock-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T20:06:30-07:00","id":261691,"title":"","content":"-Changeling: The Dreaming: It didn't fully fit in with the rest of the OWoD setting. I'd prefer if they used C:tL's concepts minus the idea that every escaped Changeling was horribly abused.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T20:16:56-07:00","id":261692,"title":"","content":"I like well written insanity though, so the abuse themes in Lost and associated disconnection of PCs are stuff I'm fond of.<br /> <br /> Still, Changeling The Lost ran in any style &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Dreaming","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T22:46:39-07:00","id":261849,"title":"","content":"Disagree with both of the above I do think that manifested Nightmares fit WoD quite perfectly. I do like Lost as well but I don't think either is superior when compared to another, just different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T07:36:46-07:00","id":262151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=261691#post261691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Changeling: The Dreaming: It didn't fully fit in with the rest of the OWoD setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least Changeling doesn't insist that exiting the atmosphere of Earth means going into the spirit world, or claim that technology is really a kind of magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd prefer if they used C:tL's concepts minus the idea that every escaped Changeling was horribly abused.<br /> </div> </div> </div>That would emphatically not be Lost in concept, since Lost is built entirely on the aftermath of escaping an abusive life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T11:30:25-07:00","id":262317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=262151#post262151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would emphatically not be Lost in concept, since Lost is built entirely on the aftermath of escaping an abusive life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T11:32:00-07:00","id":262320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least Changeling doesn't insist that exiting the atmosphere of Earth means going into the spirit world, or claim that technology is really a kind of magic. </div> </div> </div>At least is Mage is relative Otherkin free.<br /> <br /> And, you know, Conventional Space extends to Asteroid belt, so none of Sleeper astronauts and cosmonauts entered Umbra <br /> <br /> As long as it's consensual it's not really Magic. Human preconceptions do shape Consensus, but as long as it's consensual it's a part of local reality and sleeper scientists who after all beat Enlightened Scientists to some of inventions don't warp reality like the latter when doing that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T12:06:11-07:00","id":262338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=262320#post262320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least is Mage is relative Otherkin free.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not an observation. It is a projection. Changeling isn't supposed to be about Otherkin, it's supposed to be about the icy clutch of forgetting wondrous, if alien, dreams. It's a different kind of loss from Lost, and can cross over into general traumatic accidents that take some capability away from you. There was more to you, once, but that's all you can recall. Nothing of what that more was. It's beyond you, now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, you know, Conventional Space extends to Asteroid belt, so none of Sleeper astronauts and cosmonauts entered Umbra </div> </div> </div>Not even the point. Mage is welcome to its take on the Umbra, just as long as no one pretends for a moment that it's supposed to mesh with other games. It's like its own setting is a giant Paradox-realm. RECURSION!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As long as it's consensual it's not really Magic. Human preconceptions do shape Consensus, but as long as it's consensual it's a part of local reality and sleeper scientists who after all beat Enlightened Scientists to some of inventions don't warp reality like the latter when doing that.<br /> </div> </div> </div>You're only proving my point! No other WoD games incorporate this metaphysical assumption. Even Changeling only uses mass belief as a feature that's more akin to a representation of peer pressure than post-modernism, and doesn't seek to paint everything as a type of magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T16:26:54-07:00","id":262535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=260617#post260617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Tremere as Mages turning into Vampires and somehow winning a war versus the WHOLE Order of Hermes, plus the Tzimisce while being based in Transylvania (Ceoris).</div> </div> </div> </div>I always took it for granted that Saulot personally intervened to make sure that Tremere survived long enough to diablerize him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T08:40:24-07:00","id":262885,"title":"","content":"The Tzimisce were probably too riddled with internecine conflict to be truly effective against an organized foe. (Plus, once the Inquisition got started, they'd have had bigger worries as the vampires who lived openly and thus made the easiest targets for torch-bearing mobs.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T11:30:03-07:00","id":262974,"title":"","content":"<br /> I will second the whole &quot;origins story&quot; of Clan Tremere as the most unbeleivable heap of handwavings and implausible allowances. No, really - how did they survive in early 1200s fighting on their own &quot;turf&quot; against local Tzims, Gangrels, Nosferatu (plus some random Shadow Lords, probably), against the whole Order of Hermes (and how they were not &quot;outed&quot; before 1201/2 by other mages), Salubri (Warriors are anything but pushovers) and Inqusition in the rest of Europe, while<br /> <br /> a) High clans don't even consider you a proper vampires and mostly treat you like shytte.<br /> b) Low clans don't even consider you a proper vampires and often want to kill you.<br /> <br /> when even their &quot;Founders&quot; are still Ancillas?<br /> <br /> The only logical, so to speak, explanation is that they have decided to mass-embrace lots and lots of peasants, tought them Thaumaturgy (Movement of the mind) to 3-4 dots and used them as un-living catapults that can with relative ease propell rocks, spears, arroves, canisters of greek fire and even a Vozhd-war ghoul at their enemies general direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=262885#post262885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimisce were probably too riddled with internecine conflict to be truly effective against an organized foe. (Plus, once the Inquisition got started, they'd have had bigger worries as the vampires who lived openly and thus made the easiest targets for torch-bearing mobs.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Inqusition (both Shadow and a real one) was virtually non-existent in Tzims hearlands. And your typical &quot;torches and pitchforks&quot; mob is nothing against a warband of &quot;flesh-crafted ghouls&quot; (I really hate using word &quot;Szlachta&quot; to call them that. It's... so wrong!), a couple of childer AND Vozhd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 09-22-2014, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T11:48:55-07:00","id":262982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, the Inqusition (both Shadow and a real one) was virtually non-existent in Tzims hearlands. And your typical &quot;torches and pitchforks&quot; mob is nothing against a warband of &quot;flesh-crafted ghouls&quot; (I really hate using word &quot;Szlachta&quot; to call them that. It's... so wrong!), a couple of childer AND Vozhd. </div> </div> </div>While activities of Inquisition in my country were relatively restrained, it still existed, and organised action coordinated by local nobles (whom V20 mentions to be involved in whole Burning Times thing, as they did not like their temporal power compromised by bloodsucking fiends) could be startingly effective.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T20:04:20-07:00","id":263348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/92008-biggest-fails-ups-d-ouhs-on-the-owod-cannon?p=262974#post262974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will second the whole &quot;origins story&quot; of Clan Tremere as the most unbeleivable heap of handwavings and implausible allowances...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like I said up above. I always took it as read that Saulot personally intervened to make sure Tremere survived long enough to diablerize him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}